---
import GuideLayout from '../layouts/GuideLayout.astro';
import { guides } from '../data/guides';
import ExemptionChecklist from '../components/ExemptionChecklist.astro';
---
<GuideLayout guide={guides[1]} heading={guides[1].name}>
  <div class="reference-answer"><p><strong>You may qualify for a Measure PFD exemption through household income, an existing Pasadena senior or disability utility-tax exemption, or qualifying property ownership.</strong> Age alone does not qualify you. Check which category may apply below.</p></div>
  <ExemptionChecklist />
  <section id="owners"><h2>Which PFD exemptions could apply to you as an owner?</h2><h3>Is there a Measure PFD senior exemption?</h3><p><strong>Yes, if you receive Pasadena’s senior citizen or disability utility-tax exemption.</strong> Being a senior, by itself, does not meet this requirement.</p><h3>Can low-income owners qualify regardless of age?</h3><p><strong>Yes.</strong> You could qualify based on income, regardless of age. Your annual household income must be at or below HUD’s Very Low (50%) Income Limit for Los Angeles-Long Beach-Glendale for the year you claim an exemption.</p></section>
  <section id="organizations"><h2>Which government and organization properties are exempt?</h2><p>Federal, state, and local government agencies would not pay this tax. Religious facilities and community-service organizations could also qualify if their property is exempt from value-based property taxes under California law.</p><p>Constitutional tax exemptions would still apply. Nonprofit or business status alone does not automatically qualify a property.</p></section>
  <section id="eligibility"><h2>How do you confirm your PFD exemption?</h2><p>Start with the owner or property category above that matches your situation. Ask the City to confirm the requirements. If Measure PFD passes, follow the City’s published application instructions and deadlines.</p><p>For the income-based exemption, check the official income limit for the year you claim it. The proposed ordinance uses that year’s limit, so a single dollar amount does not apply to every household or year.</p><p><a href="/measure-pfd-calculator/">Calculate your PFD tax before exemptions</a>.</p></section>
</GuideLayout>
